WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.642 --> 00:00:03.309
(opera singing)

00:00:09.097 --> 00:00:11.879
- Music is one of those things
that just reaches people,

00:00:11.879 --> 00:00:14.208
and I feel like opera specifically

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:16.541
has that effect on everyone.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.579
It's pure, it's raw, and it's beautiful.

00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:25.160
I do feel like we're making
it so everyone can enjoy it.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.410
(applause)

00:00:30.548 --> 00:00:32.893
(orchestral music)

00:00:32.893 --> 00:00:35.300
My name is Alexis Cregger,
and I'm an opera singer

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.121
and a member of the Opera Collective.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:40.204
We're about 30 right now.

00:00:42.605 --> 00:00:45.357
We come together two to three times a week

00:00:45.357 --> 00:00:46.955
to bring opera to the people.

00:00:46.955 --> 00:00:48.470
(opera singing)

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.131
We sing in the subways of New York City.

00:00:50.131 --> 00:00:54.298
My mom used to always listen
to the Met broadcasts.

00:00:55.986 --> 00:00:59.647
When I was 14, she took me to
the Met for the first time

00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:01.672
and Queen of the Night came on stage

00:01:01.672 --> 00:01:05.839
and I saw her, and I said,
"That's what I wanna do."

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.601
(opera singing)

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:16.318
Most people do have that
initial feeling of oh, opera.

00:01:16.318 --> 00:01:17.315
I don't like opera.

00:01:17.315 --> 00:01:18.898
What is this opera?

00:01:20.028 --> 00:01:22.206
But bringing opera to the subway

00:01:22.206 --> 00:01:24.677
really makes it for everyone

00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:27.942
and it really makes it
something that people feel like

00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:29.775
they can connect with.

00:01:35.542 --> 00:01:39.780
It's one of those places where
people just go by every day

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.918
(applause)

00:01:40.918 --> 00:01:42.929
all day long, and so you really get to see

00:01:42.929 --> 00:01:44.596
all walks of people.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:48.419
(cheering)

00:01:48.419 --> 00:01:50.901
(piano music)

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:54.323
We've had people come and stand or sit

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:57.990
for practically the
entire time we're there.

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:00.973
We had a note that was given to us

00:02:00.973 --> 00:02:05.152
by a girl who was really not
doing that well that day.

00:02:05.152 --> 00:02:06.833
She was sitting on one of the benches

00:02:06.833 --> 00:02:11.000
and she was there for
probably close to two hours.

00:02:12.242 --> 00:02:13.864
At the end of it, she came up

00:02:13.864 --> 00:02:18.031
and put this note along with
some change into the bucket.

00:02:20.415 --> 00:02:21.794
Basically she had said

00:02:21.794 --> 00:02:24.463
that she had been contemplating suicide

00:02:24.463 --> 00:02:27.838
and listening to us, sitting
there and hearing that music

00:02:27.838 --> 00:02:30.255
it just, it changed her mind.

00:02:31.705 --> 00:02:33.538
That's why we do this.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.412
(applause)

00:02:37.412 --> 00:02:41.636
I'm so happy that we can
make that sort of impact.

00:02:41.636 --> 00:02:44.136
It's a really beautiful thing.

